  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bc4ea96c-289d-4a5d-97c1-1ca07043df2f",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5168,
        1360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Retry failed OpenAI calls with Anthropic fallback and cost logging in Data Tables\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow accepts an LLM prompt from chat or from another workflow, builds a provider-specific request, and routes it to OpenAI first or Anthropic as a fallback. It classifies each response, retries transient failures with a wait delay, switches providers when needed, then builds a final result. It records the outcome and cost details in n8n Data Tables, sends a Telegram alert on final failure, and returns the result to the caller.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the OpenAI and Anthropic API credentials or HTTP headers used by the provider request nodes.\n- Update the reliability settings node with the desired prompt inputs, system prompt, primary provider, primary model, retry limits, and fallback behavior.\n- Ensure the n8n Data Table used for call logging exists or that the workflow has permission to create it, with fields matching the logged cost/status data.\n- Configure Telegram bot credentials and the destination chat ID for failure alerts.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the retry delay, retry classification rules, provider/model selection, and cost calculation logic to match your reliability and budget requirements."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
